UID:10119-1789822800-1789830000@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Flow Into Form:  A Qi Gong and Expressive Art Experience
DESCRIPTION:Saturday September 19 | 1 – 3 pm\, $40  \nBreathe. Move. Create. \nFacilitated by Niraj Shah – long-time qi-gong teacher and practitioner\, and Naz Botas – artist and owner of the Space. \nIf you’ve been craving a gentle reset—something grounding\, nourishing\, and expressive—this workshop is your invitation. \nIn this two-hour workshop\, you’ll move through repeating cycles of Qi Gong and intuitive art-making designed to calm your nervous system\, soften tension in the body\, and open your creative heart. \nYou’ll experience: \n\nQi Gong: slow\, mindful movements paired with gentle breathwork to flow your energy and bring you into the present moment\nIntuitive Art: using charcoal\, ink\, or pastels\, you’ll make marks on wall-length paper as your body moves — both naturally and through guided Qi Gong sequences — allowing your inner experience to express itself visually\n\nAcross the session\, we’ll repeat several short rounds of movement followed by mark-making\, gradually building comfort\, curiosity\, and expression. By the end\, you’ll be able to look at your paper and literally see the journey your body and breath took you on. \nNo prior experience in art or Qi Gong is needed. Just a willingness to breathe\, move\, and let the paper receive whatever wants to come through. \nExpect a peaceful\, meditative atmosphere.\nA safe space.\nAnd a sense of release you’ll carry with you long after the workshop ends. \nThese practices help you: \n\nLet go of stress stored in the body\nFeel more present and grounded\nReconnect with your authentic creativity\nExpress yourself without pressure or judgment\n\nA beautiful experience for anyone seeking clarity\, calm\, and creative freedom! \nWhat to Bring: \n\ncomfortable clothing you can move in\na water bottle\nan open heart and curious mind
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/flow-into-form-a-qi-gong-and-expressive-art-experience/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Meditate and Create,Meditation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/20260124_154132-scaled-e1775574481620.jpg
END:VEVENT
